# Build output. Regenerated deterministically by `npm run ship`, and a 1.3 MB
# generated file rewritten on every release would bloat history for no benefit.
dist/

# Dependencies. This project has none at runtime; nothing here should appear.
node_modules/

# Local preview and editor cruft
.DS_Store
*.log
.vercel/
.idea/
.vscode/

# NOTE ON WHAT IS DELIBERATELY *NOT* IGNORED
#
# data/ and public/data/ are tracked on purpose. They are the indexed layer, and
# .github/workflows/refresh.yml commits them after each scheduled run — that is
# how the deployed site gets fresh data. Regenerating them costs thousands of
# upstream requests and roughly twenty minutes.
#
# data/kaleidoscope-cache.json is tracked for the same reason. It is nominally a
# cache, but rate limiting is a real and documented failure mode here (a throttled
# run once wrote a broken leaderboard over a good one), so carrying the cache
# between CI runs is worth more than a slimmer repository. Revisit if history
# growth becomes a problem.
